c9996b96-6e07-4d46-ae97-8250d16bb402	60186569-a432-4375-9bee-485c69f086d5	4c073a7a-7864-4341-85ce-869914b3c117	\N	FACILITY_PLAYER_DISPLACEMENT_SLAS.pdf	GLOBAL ACADEMY ATHLETE EXPERIENCE & DISPLACEMENT MANDATES ======================================================================== Document ID: SLA-2026-V1 | Section: Reservation Disruption Mitigation This document governs the automated routing protocols whenever an active tennis court asset must be taken offline due to unexpected maintenance locks or safety hazards. SECTION 1: COURT RE-ASSIGNMENT HIERARCHY When a reservation is disrupted due to a court closure, the system must immediately attempt to displace the affected players to an available court within the same facility branch using the following priority criteria: 1. Match Tier Tiering: Members must be re-routed to a court matching their exact original surface tier type (e.g., Clay to Clay, Indoor Hard to Indoor Hard). 2. Upgrade Protocol: If an identical surface type is unavailable, the player must be automatically upgraded to a higher-tier surface (e.g., Outdoor Hard upgraded to Premium Indoor Synergy Court) at no additional charge. 3. Priority Allocation: Premium Club Members hold absolute displacement priority over standard public court bookings. If an open court is available, the Premium Member's booking must be shifted instantly. SECTION 2: COMPENSATION COMPENSATION CONTINGENCIES If the facility branch is running at 100% capacity and no physical courts are available for re-routing within 60 minutes of the original booking time slot, the system must issue an automated account balance credit voucher. Standard guest vouchers are capped at $45.00, while VIP/Premium Member compensation accounts must be credited exactly $75.00 for displacement violations.	1	[-0.017486572,0.084472656,0.07647705,0.027511597,-0.0048980713,0.008872986,-0.026351929,-0.045013428,-0.014556885,-0.008041382,0.051330566,-0.01007843,0.012420654,0.031951904,0.008895874,0.0049438477,0.0150