ad3b6e14-dc79-40b0-a1a5-7cf7b989ec7d	60186569-a432-4375-9bee-485c69f086d5	59ccf6a4-094f-46ac-a272-06fec5d4ab7a	\N	ENVIRONMENTAL_AND_INSURANCE_COMPLIANCE.pdf	SPORTS RISK MANAGEMENT INC. — LIABILITY INSURANCE COMPLIANCE MANDATES ======================================================================== Policy Scope: GL-66182-04 | Audit Schedule: Real-Time Telemetry Check This manual outlines the mandatory environmental guardrails and risk mitigation scales required to maintain active general liability insurance coverage for indoor athletic enclosures. SECTION 7: CLIMATE ENVIRONMENT CONTROL REGISTRY To mitigate player slip risks, structural backdrop degradation, and athletic respiratory hazards, every indoor tennis structure operated under the academy license must comply with strict real-time telemetry sensor limits: 1. Ambient Humidity Ceiling: The relative ambient atmospheric humidity inside any indoor playing envelope must never exceed a maximum ceiling threshold of 65.0%. If an indoor sensor registers a humidity scaling above 65.0% for more than 4 consecutive hours, the court environment is classified as a 'Slip_and_Fall_Liability_Zone'. 2. Active Audit Consequences: Any facility branch operating outside these boundaries fails compliance metrics. The agent must instantly flag the violating branch on the administrative board, notify operations, and recommend an immediate HVAC system check to prevent insurance coverage suspension.	1	[0.0027122498,0.07733154,0.058288574,0.019561768,-0.016235352,0.04953003,0.00029563904,-0.06274414,-0.0019044876,0.021011353,0.04333496,-0.02848816,0.00029277802,0.007881165,0.0060691833,-0.035949707,0.030700684,0.023605347,-0.032196045,0.033081055,0.03353882,0.07287598,-0.023544312,1.680851e-05,-0.03741455,-0.03363037,0.016723633,-0.03378296,0.06402588,0.030899048,0.06201172,-0.019180298,-0.012535095,-0.033416748,0.04940796,-0.009750366,-0.009666443,0.029418945,0.011383057,-0.025115967,0.03543091,-0.0009737015,-0.030349731,0.027770996,-0.0