3913f3b9-eb53-4cff-a449-76fa1823bc39	60186569-a432-4375-9bee-485c69f086d5	4c073a7a-7864-4341-85ce-869914b3c117	\N	FACILITY_LIGHTING_PROCUREMENT_MANDATES.pdf	GLOBAL ACADEMY INDUSTRIAL LIGHTING MAINTENANCE & PARTS PROCUREMENT POLICY ======================================================================== Document Ref: PROC-LIGHTING-2026 | Authorization Code: AUTH-9942 This operational manual defines the authorized replacement materials, vendor catalog SKUs, and purchasing thresholds for all stadium, court, and facility indoor/outdoor luminaires. SECTION 1: APPROVED LIGHTING MAINTENANCE MATERIAL MATRICES When a lighting asset drops beneath the mandated safety lux thresholds due to component aging, filament exhaustion, or ballast degradation, groundskeepers and automated systems MUST strictly utilize parts conforming to the following official catalog descriptions: 1. Ballast System Failures: For court electrical sub-stations experiencing severe luminaire intensity loss, the authorized replacement assembly part text description MUST literally be registered in procurement logs as: 'Industrial High-Output Lux Ballast Assembly Part B' Utilizing non-industrial ballasts, unshielded transformers, or unapproved residential electrical hardware is strictly prohibited and violates active insurance coverage. 2. Luminaire Filament Failures: For localized light array outages where specific bulb pods have blown, the authorized procurement part description is: '750W Quartz-Halogen High-Density Pod Element' SECTION 2: AUTOMATED FISCAL SPENDING CAPS The automated AI procurement system is authorized to instantly generate Work Orders and approve Purchase Orders (PO) for lighting parts up to a maximum financial ceiling of $1,200.00 per physical court asset row. Any generation exceeding $1,200.00 will fail auto-approval and be held for 'Pending_Executive_Signoff'.	1	[-0.012825012,0.025497437,0.031707764,-0.01398468,-0.005214691,-0.0018701553,-0.031051636,-0.06719971,0.0026302338,-0.01953125,